2026-10-09T17:22:57.0011912Z -- v4.0.5 — one marginal COP per store, shared with the dynamics
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0012167Z   ok   marginal_cop('buffer') is the simulate step's own conversion
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0012333Z   ok   marginal_cop('dhw') is compute_cop_dhw
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0012639Z   ok   building-mass stores heat at the plain curve
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0012952Z   ok   without the Carnot derate the buffer collapses to the plain curve
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0013394Z   ok   the terminal credit repays a stored buffer kWh at the flow-derated COP the simulation charged to store it, less what the tank loses first
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0013659Z   ok   and at -5 C that haircut is small: winter storage is not discouraged
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0013931Z   ok   which is genuinely dearer than the plain curve the old code paid
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0014107Z   ok   building-mass deficits keep the plain conversion
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0014428Z   ok   derate off: the terminal term is the historical single-sum, exactly
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0014777Z   ok   a DHW deficit settles at compute_cop_dhw of its settlement temperature
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0015052Z   ok   and a buffer deficit at the flow-derated COP of its settlement ceiling
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0015061Z 
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0015380Z -- v4.0.5 — settlement caps: the lower zone's slab, a reachable tank
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0015621Z   ok   two-zone slab cap is sized from the lower zone alone
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0015892Z   ok   and it moves with the learned split, like the dynamics it settles
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0016077Z   ok   single-zone keeps the historical formula exactly
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0016392Z   ok   a strong pump's cap is the rating — mild installs are untouched
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0016693Z   ok   a weak pump against a cold day cannot reach the rating, and the cap says so
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0016933Z   ok   the reachable ceiling rises with milder weather, up to the rating
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0017003Z 
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0017332Z -- v4.0.5 — DHW conservation: a cold tank cannot pour hot water
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0017558Z   ok   the booked draw never exceeds the nominal demand
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0017761Z   ok   every step balances: in == out + losses + storage delta
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0018069Z   ok   the inlet floor fabricated nothing — the scaled draw makes it inert
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0018347Z   ok   a cold tank delivers less than the nominal demand, not the same
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0018559Z   ok   and the tank never pins to the inlet pouring imaginary heat
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0018798Z   ok   a tank at the setpoint is debited exactly the nominal draw
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0019083Z   ok   charging cannot pass the tank rating, and the excess is booked
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0019302Z   ok   a tank read above the rating cools at its physical rate, not by fiat
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0019603Z   ok   an inlet above the tank's surroundings manufactures no heat over 24 h
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0019878Z   ok   the tank is not pinned at the inlet: it settles toward its surroundings
2026-10-09T17:22:57.0020102Z   ok   coil split at the default inlet is the historical arithmetic
